# apps/web patterns

## Layout

- Routes: `app/(dashboard)/{overview,profile,applications,resumes,interviews,settings}/page.tsx`
- UI: `components/{domain}/` · Primitives: `components/ui/` (shadcn)
- Domain logic: `lib/{domain}/queries.ts` (read) + `actions.ts` (mutate)

## Data flow

- **Server Components** in `page.tsx` fetch via `queries.ts`
- **Client components** call server actions from `actions.ts`; use `revalidatePath` in actions after mutations
- Supabase server client: `lib/supabase/server.ts` · Service role (extension API only): `lib/supabase/service.ts`

## Server actions (`"use server"`)

- One `"use server"` file per domain at `lib/{domain}/actions.ts`
- Profile is split: implementations in `lib/profile/actions/*`, **async wrappers only** in `lib/profile/actions.ts` (Next.js cannot re-export from `"use server"` barrels)
- Do not export types from `"use server"` files — put shared types in `lib/{domain}/types.ts` or `@hirevault/types`

## Key URLs

| Surface | Route / param |
|---------|----------------|
| Applications board | `/applications` or `?view=board` (default) |
| Applications list | `?view=list` |
| Resumes index | `/resumes` (no `application` param) |
| Resume builder | `/resumes?application=<id>&version=<n>` |
| Interview prep | `/interviews?job=<id>` |

Use `resumeBuilderUrl(applicationId)` — do not hand-build resume query strings.

## Common pitfalls (see docs/OPERATIONS.md)

- Empty states must still show entry points (add application, pick application, etc.)
- Child lists must filter by parent scope (`jobId`, `applicationId`) — no cross-scope leakage

## Extension API

`app/api/extension/capture/route.ts` — bearer auth via `lib/extension/auth.ts`, field merge via `lib/extension/merge-capture-fields.ts`
